WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:14.321
A lot of Samantha's friends wore glasses.

2
00:00:15.342 --> 00:00:17.223
Henry's glasses made him look smart.

3
00:00:20.164 --> 00:00:22.385
Glasses made shy Emma stand out.

4
00:00:23.745 --> 00:00:25.826
Jenna had several pairs of glasses.

5
00:00:27.547 --> 00:00:29.548
She liked her glasses to match her clothes!

6
00:00:32.104 --> 00:00:35.026
Samantha wanted to look smarter and more stylish too.

7
00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:42.491
"Mom," said Samantha.

8
00:00:42.511 --> 00:00:45.013
"I need glasses."

9
00:00:45.033 --> 00:00:48.475
"Do you have trouble seeing at school?"

10
00:00:48.836 --> 00:00:49.416
asked Mom.

11
00:00:49.436 --> 00:00:52.218
"Um," said Samantha quickly.

12
00:00:52.238 --> 00:01:00.644
"Sometimes." "I'll make an appointment to see the optometrist," said Mom.

13
00:01:04.936 --> 00:01:06.617
Samantha and Mom went to Dr.

14
00:01:06.677 --> 00:01:08.098
Green's office the next day.

15
00:01:10.759 --> 00:01:11.940
Samantha felt bad.

16
00:01:14.081 --> 00:01:15.542
She thought she could see fine.

17
00:01:18.003 --> 00:01:19.624
She just wanted glasses!

18
00:01:21.525 --> 00:01:25.067
Dr. Green asked Samantha to read a chart with rows of letters.

19
00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:30.610
It wasn't easy!

20
00:01:31.251 --> 00:01:33.772
The letters at the bottom looked small and blurry.

21
00:01:35.068 --> 00:01:35.989
She couldn't read them.

22
00:01:37.570 --> 00:01:40.493
Dr. Green sat down to talk to Samantha and Mom.

23
00:01:42.414 --> 00:01:44.636
"You're nearsighted, Samantha," said Dr.

24
00:01:44.676 --> 00:01:47.819
Green. "What does that mean?"

25
00:01:48.159 --> 00:01:48.960
asked Samantha.

26
00:01:49.881 --> 00:01:53.183
She wanted glasses, but she didn't want problems with her vision!

27
00:01:53.203 --> 00:01:59.849
"Nearsighted people see things close up normally," said Dr.

28
00:01:59.889 --> 00:02:03.172
Green. "But faraway things look blurry."

29
00:02:05.728 --> 00:02:08.470
Dr. Green showed them a model of a round eyeball.

30
00:02:10.051 --> 00:02:14.333
"The eyeball in nearsighted people is a little too long," he explained.

31
00:02:14.353 --> 00:02:18.635
"In farsighted people the eyeball is too short."

32
00:02:21.297 --> 00:02:23.578
"Is this because Samantha reads so much?"

33
00:02:24.078 --> 00:02:24.679
asked Mom.

34
00:02:24.699 --> 00:02:28.661
"Too much reading doesn't cause the problem.

35
00:02:29.241 --> 00:02:33.364
But it's good to take breaks to avoid eye strain or headaches," said Dr.

36
00:02:33.404 --> 00:02:39.920
Green. "Being nearsighted can be caused by family history or the environment," Dr.

37
00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:40.761
Green continued.

38
00:02:40.781 --> 00:02:45.705
"I heard eating carrots helps you see," said Samantha.

39
00:02:45.725 --> 00:02:50.850
"Carrots and oily fish like salmon have vitamin A," said Dr.

40
00:02:50.890 --> 00:02:54.513
Green. "So do dark leafy vegetables.

41
00:02:55.874 --> 00:02:57.876
Vitamin A helps keep eyes healthy."

42
00:02:57.896 --> 00:03:00.839
"Will it fix my eyes?"

43
00:03:01.359 --> 00:03:02.160
asked Samantha.

44
00:03:03.976 --> 00:03:05.537
"It won't cure your eyes."

45
00:03:05.897 --> 00:03:07.138
Dr. Green smiled.

46
00:03:10.279 --> 00:03:12.440
"Spend more time outdoors in the sunshine.

47
00:03:14.201 --> 00:03:17.763
Scientists believe that it slows children's eyes from becoming nearsighted.

48
00:03:19.484 --> 00:03:22.005
For now, glasses will help you see clearly."

49
00:03:26.027 --> 00:03:27.768
Samantha chose her new glasses.

50
00:03:37.376 --> 00:03:38.617
"I look great!"

51
00:03:39.057 --> 00:03:39.497
she said.

52
00:03:45.980 --> 00:03:46.981
I can see better!"

53
00:03:47.001 --> 00:03:51.383
"Let me see how you look," said Mom.

54
00:03:53.884 --> 00:03:56.305
She squinted and then leaned closer to Samantha.

55
00:04:00.207 --> 00:04:02.208
You do look good," said Mom.

56
00:04:05.985 --> 00:04:08.845
"But maybe I need to make an appointment for myself!"
